{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Behold, your days draw near to die.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): Scripture teaches you that the life of man is decreed, and each person has fixed days, and the Holy One, blessed be He, brings a person's days to the appointed and decreed time, as it is said (Exodus 23:26): ״את מספר ימיך אמלא״. And this language of drawing near is mentioned concerning the righteous: (Genesis 47:29) ״ויקרבו ימי ישראל למות״, (I Kings 2:1) ״ויקרבו ימי דוד למות״, and this indicates that a person's life is decreed, and He, blessed be He, fills it and brings it near to the fixed and decreed time, or extends it beyond what was decreed according to merit, or shortens it from what was decreed according to punishment. And according to what is known, that the Holy One, blessed be He, fixed in the firmament the courses of the stars and gave them power to produce effects in the lower realm, and they in their course bring benefit and harm in this world, and everything depends on the mazal (celestial lot) — for the Sages of the Talmud, of blessed memory, did not deny and refute this influence, but rather there was among them a glorious wisdom concerning it, and they explicitly said in Mo'ed Katan at the end of the chapter Eleh Megalchin: 'Children, life, and sustenance are not dependent on merit, but on the mazal.' And they brought a proof for this and said: 'Know this, for Rav and Rav Hisda were both righteous; one lived forty years and the other lived sixty years; in the house of one there were sixty wedding celebrations, and in the house of the other sixty mourning services; in the house of one, even barley bread for the members of his household was not to be found, while in the house of the other, fine wheat bread was not even demanded for the dog.' And this is a complete proof that they acknowledge this wisdom, and so too the truth, for the Omnipresent gave them the power at the time of their creation to benefit and to harm, but He, blessed be He, despite having delivered to them the power to act upon the lower realm — His power, blessed be He, remains supreme over all and was not withdrawn from Him, and in His hand to humble the high and to exalt the low, to fulfill what was decreed and to add to what was decreed and to diminish from it. And so too regarding the years of a person, He brings the days of his life near to the decreed time and fills them, as it is said (Exodus 23:26): ״את מספר ימיך אמלא״; and He extends them beyond what was decreed, as with Hezekiah, of whom it is said (Isaiah 38:5): ״הנני יוסיף על ימיך חמש עשרה שנה״ — and the addition is only upon what was fixed and decreed at first, for He said that the Omnipresent added to him fifteen (ט״ו) years beyond what was decreed. And He shortens them from what was decreed, as with Ahaziah the son of Ahab king of Israel, who fell ill and went to inquire through idolatry, and He shortened his days, as it is said (II Kings 1:16): ״יען אשר שלחת מלאכים לדרוש בבעל זבוב אלהי עקרון המבלי אין אלהים בישראל לדרוש בדברו לכן המטה אשר עלית שם לא תרד ממנה כי מות תמות״ — and this verse testifies that the cause of his death was his inquiry through idolatry, for if death had been decreed upon him from the start, what did the prophet come to inform him? You thus learn that the Holy One, blessed be He, fills a person's days and brings them near to the decreed time, and likewise extends them beyond what was decreed and shortens them from what was decreed — all according to His will, for therefore is He called Shaddai, because He breaks (משדד) the celestial array and overcomes it, and all according to reward and punishment. If so, the explanation of the statement 'Children, life, and sustenance are not dependent on merit but on the mazal' is that it comes to inform us how great is the power of prayer, for since the power of the Omnipresent is supreme over all and was not withdrawn from Him, He is able and it is easy for Him to nullify the great power He delivered to them. For the masters of astronomy, who gaze at the stars, acknowledge this with arguments that the Holy One, blessed be He, is the general principle and the configuration of the stars is the particular, and the general is greater than the particular and can nullify its power. And in everything decreed regarding human contingencies through the power of the celestial array, it is possible for a person to nullify it through his merit without prayer and without crying out at all, but rather he need only be troubled and pained in his heart, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 145:19): ״רצון יראיו יעשה״ — that is, He fulfills the desires of their heart without their asking at all. But in these three matters, prayer and crying out are required, and this is what it says (ibid.): ״ואת שועתם ישמע ויושיעם״, and with prayer and crying out they will be granted to him. For so we find that all three were given through the merit of prayer: children were given to Rachel, as it is said (Genesis 30:22): ״וישמע אליה אלהים ויפתח את רחמה״; life to Hezekiah, as it is said (Isaiah 38:5): ״שמעתי את תפלתך הנני יוסיף על ימיך חמש עשרה שנה״; sustenance to Elijah and Elisha, for we find concerning them that sustenance was multiplied and they were saved from famine. And because of this the Sages aroused us concerning these three that depend on the mazal, and informed us that abundant prayer will be needed in them, and with prayer the power of the mazal will be nullified, just as it was nullified in all three of them through prayer." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: <b>Behold, your days draw near to die.</b> Moses said before the Holy One, blessed be He: Master of the Universe! With 'הן' I praised You, as it is said (Deuteronomy 10:14): ״הן לה' אלהיך השמים ושמי השמים״ — and with 'הן' You decree death upon me! To what is the matter compared? To a king who had a great minister whom he loved exceedingly, and that minister saw a beautiful sword unequaled in its beauty. He said: 'This is worthy for the king.' What did he do? He acquired it and gave it to the king. The king said: 'Let them sever his head with it.' So said Moses: Master of the Universe! With the offering that I brought You, You prosecute me with it! And furthermore, <b>הן קרבו ימיך למות</b> may also include: the sun has drawn near to set, and the dominion of the moon has come — and this alludes to the rank of Moses and the rank of Joshua, the one being likened to the sun and the other to the moon. And this is what the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: <b>הנך שוכב</b> … <b>וקם</b> — that is, even though you lie with your fathers, the power that is the source of the excellence of your prophecy — it endures and stands, to illuminate the moon, just as the setting sun does not set except to illuminate the moon. And this is the sense of <b>ואצונו</b>, for the commandment is the Oral Torah, which is the power of the moon, and therefore it says <b>ואצונו</b> — 'I will cause My power to flow into the moon.'" "<b>And Moses went, and Joshua.</b> He went from the camp of Israel to the camp of the Shekhinah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "Lemma rendered as 'ואצונו' per the Hebrew text, though the word in Deut. 31:14 is וצוהו; this appears to be the author's own shortened/variant form."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:59.185749259Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}